# The repository is split into workspaces; each one has its own example file:
#
#   server/.env.example   -> copy to server/.env        (API, database, auth secrets, Redis, jobs)
#   client/.env.example   -> copy to client/.env.local  (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL only)
#
# A root .env is still read by the server as a fallback, but new setups should use
# server/.env. Never commit .env files. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
